Cyde Weys <vze23tnc@verizon.net> writes:
> What exactly is the penalty for attacking peaceful monsters?
> 
> I do it all the time and I'm wondering if I shouldn't.

* A Samurai will always suffer a -1 alignment penalty (not below -10)
* If the monster is not paralysed, missing will anger it, incurring a
  -1 alignment penalty (-5 for coaligned priests, +2 _bonus_ for
  cross-aligned priests)
* Hitting the monster will anger it, paralysed or not, with the results as
  above.

Actually _killing_ the monster may have further consequences, but
those are the considerations for attacking it; also, attacking the
monster may have consequences not dependent on its peacful status
(such as the "caitiff" penalty for Knights). This is also only
considering melee combat attacks.

